      <!-- Part 1: What is a REST API? -->
      <div style="margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">
        <span style="font-size: 0.6875rem; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.05em; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
          Part 1: What is a REST API?
        </span>

        <!-- Restaurant Analogy Box -->
        <div style="background: var(--bg-subtle); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          <strong style="color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 0.8125rem; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
            🍽️ The Restaurant Analogy:
          </strong>
          <ul style="list-style: none; font-size: 0.78125rem; color: var(--text-secondary); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; margin: 0; padding-left: 0.5rem;">
            <li>&bull; <strong>You (Client / Frontend SPA):</strong> You sit at the table and want food, but you cannot walk into the private kitchen.</li>
            <li>&bull; <strong>The Kitchen (Backend &amp; Database):</strong> Where sensitive data is stored, calculated, and prepared securely.</li>
            <li>&bull; <strong>The Waiter (The REST API):</strong> Takes your request (<code class="code-pill">GET /menu</code>), delivers it to the kitchen, and returns your food on a standard plate (<strong>JSON Data</strong>).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem;">
          <div>
            <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Core Principles of REST:</strong>
            <ul style="list-style: none; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; padding-left: 0.25rem;">
              <li>&bull; <strong>Stateless:</strong> Every request is self-contained. The server does not store session memory between requests; authentication is carried in the token (<code class="code-pill">Authorization: Bearer &lt;JWT&gt;</code>).</li>
              <li>&bull; <strong>Standard HTTP Verbs:</strong>
                <div style="margin-top: 0.2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.2rem;">
                  <span><code class="code-pill">GET</code> Read / Retrieve (e.g., balance inquiry)</span>
                  <span><code class="code-pill">POST</code> Create new records (e.g., fund transfers)</span>
                  <span><code class="code-pill">PUT</code> Update existing records (e.g., unlock user)</span>
                  <span><code class="code-pill">DELETE</code> Remove records (e.g., delete beneficiary)</span>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-primary); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Standard JSON Response Format:</strong>
            <div style="background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); padding: 0.75rem;">
              <pre style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.75rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); overflow-x: auto; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45;">
{`{
  "responseCode": "000",
  "message": "Transfer successful",
  "transactionId": "TXN-2026-98124",
  "amount": 50000.00
}`}
              </pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Part 2: Architecture Comparison Diagram & Table -->
      <div style="margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">
        <span style="font-size: 0.6875rem; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.05em; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
          Part 2: Serverless REST API vs. Traditional Web Server (Tomcat / XAMPP)
        </span>

        <!-- ASCII Architecture Comparison -->
        <div style="background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--radius-xs); padding: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          <pre style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.71875rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); overflow-x: auto; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.4;">
{`TRADITIONAL (Tomcat / XAMPP):
+--------------------------------------------------------+
| Server Machine (VM or Physical Box)                   |
|   +------------------------------------------------+   |
|   | Apache Tomcat / Apache HTTP (Runs 24/7/365)    |   |  <-- Consumes RAM/CPU
|   |   - All APIs bundled into 1 big .WAR file      |   |      even if 0 requests
|   |   - Handles threads, connection pools, memory  |   |      arrive at 3:00 AM
|   +------------------------------------------------+   |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

SERVERLESS (Azure Functions Java in admin_console):
Request Ingress --> [HTTP Trigger] 
                          |
             (Spins up in milliseconds)
                          v
               +----------------------+
               | Function Execution   |  <-- Runs ONLY for the duration
               | @FunctionName("...") |      of the request (e.g., 200ms),
               +----------------------+      then shuts down
                          |
                (0 Cost / 0 RAM at idle)`}
          </pre>
        </div>

        <!-- Detailed Comparison Table -->
        <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
          <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.8125rem; text-align: left;">
            <thead>
              <tr style="background: var(--bg-subtle); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
                <th style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); width: 180px;">Dimension</th>
                <th style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Traditional REST API (Apache Tomcat / XAMPP)</th>
                <th style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent-emerald);">Serverless REST API (Azure Functions in admin_console)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">How it Runs</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">A long-running background process (<code class="code-pill">catalina.sh run</code> or <code class="code-pill">httpd</code>) that stays alive constantly in memory.</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Event-Driven:</strong> Wakes up only when an HTTP request arrives, executes, and terminates.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Idle Resource Usage</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>High:</strong> Consumes 2GB–8GB of RAM and CPU even at midnight when nobody is using the system.</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Zero:</strong> Consumes 0 CPU and 0 active memory when there are no requests.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Deployment Package</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">Heavy monolithic archive (<code class="code-pill">.war</code> or <code class="code-pill">.jar</code>) deployed into Tomcat's <code class="code-pill">webapps/</code> directory.</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">Lightweight individual function classes packaged via Maven (<code class="code-pill">mvn package</code>).</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Scaling Capability</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Manual / Complex:</strong> You must provision extra VMs and configure load balancers to handle traffic spikes.</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Automatic Elasticity:</strong> If 10 requests arrive, 10 functions run. If 5,000 burst in at month-end, the cloud fabric spins up 5,000 instances automatically.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);">
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Failure Isolation</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Shared Blast Radius:</strong> If one API has a memory leak (<code class="code-pill">OutOfMemoryError</code>), the entire Tomcat server crashes, taking down all APIs.</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Isolated:</strong> Each function runs in its own execution sandbox. A crash in one endpoint never crashes other endpoints.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);">Cost Model</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">Pay for the server hardware/VM 24 hours a day, 30 days a month, regardless of traffic.</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">Pay strictly per execution millisecond (e.g., pay for 250 milliseconds per API invocation).</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

